        "\n",
        "sweep_id = \"bi1qfge3\"\n",
        "\n",
        "sweep = api.sweep(f\"{project}/{sweep_id}\")\n",
        "\n",
        "runs = sweep.runs\n",
        "\n",
        "records = []\n",
        "\n",
        "for run in runs:\n",
        "    record = {\n",
        "        \"k1\": run.config.get(\"k1\"),\n",
        "        \"b\": run.config.get(\"b\"),\n",
        "        \"recall\": run.summary.get(\"val_recall@10\"),\n",
        "        \"mrr\": run.summary.get(\"val_rr@10\"),\n",
        "        \"ndcg10\": run.summary.get(\"val_ndcg@10\"),\n",
        "        \"ndcg100\": run.summary.get(\"val_ndcg@100\"),\n",
        "        \"ndcg1000\": run.summary.get(\"val_ndcg@1000\"),\n",
        "        \"candidate_recall\": run.summary.get(\"val_candidate_recall\")\n",
        "    }\n",
        "    records.append(record)\n",
        "\n",
        "df = pd.DataFrame(records)\n",
        "df_sorted = df.sort_values(by=\"candidate_recall\", ascending=False)\n",
        "df_sorted"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 29,
      "metadata": {
        "id": "sJWFYeSTNGcD"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "best_bm25 = pt.BatchRetrieve(\n",
        "    index,\n",
        "    wmodel=\"BM25\",\n",
        "    num_results=10000,\n",
        "    controls={\"bm25.k_1\": 0.9, \"bm25.b\": 0.9}\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "bm25_val_candidates = best_bm25.transform(val_queries_pt)\n",
        "\n",
        "bm25_val_candidates = bm25_val_candidates.rename(columns={\n",
        "    \"qid\": \"query_id\",\n",
        "    \"docno\": \"doc_id\"\n",
        "})\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "bm25_val_candidates[\"query_id\"] = bm25_val_candidates[\"query_id\"].astype(str)\n",
        "bm25_val_candidates[\"doc_id\"] = bm25_val_candidates[\"doc_id\"].astype(str)\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "eNxKVLTOvy7o"
      },
      "source": [
        "the best result is:\n",
        "\n",
        "An investigation into BM25 with varying values of k1 and b was done by performing a sweep over these two parameters using the validation dataset where the number of candidates was kept constant at 10000. It was seen from the results obtained that higher values of b and k1 produced better result. (k1=0.9, b=0.9). 10000 was chosen to make balance between computation and getting good result. (Despite the recall of candidates rising until 20,000, high-ranked criteria like Recall@10, MRR@10, and nDCG@10 did not change beyond 10,000. It means that 10,000 candidates were considered a reasonable number of candidates based on computation time and document retrieval.)\n",
        "\n",
        "(Since BM25 is mainly used as a candidate generator for later SBERT and BGE-M3 reranking, the hyperparameter selection prioritized candidate recall rather than top-10 ranking metrics. When candidate recall was tied, nDCG@10 was used as a secondary criterion.)\n",
        "\n",
        "# BGE-M3"
      ]
    },
